course: dictionary
lesson: 2590
title: Denticles: tiny tooth-like scales
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name very small parts of living things. «Shark skin is covered in tiny tooth-like scales called denticles.» Tiny tells you the scales are very small, and tooth-like tells you they look a bit like teeth.
explain: Scientists also call them «dermal denticles». Dermal means to do with the skin, so a dermal denticle is a tiny tooth-like scale in the skin.
explain: The other sentence gives more clues: denticles «feel smooth one way and like sandpaper the other». Use those clues to picture the word, then check your meaning by putting it into the sentence.
fact: A denticle is a tiny tooth-like scale or bump.
fact: Shark skin is covered in denticles that point backwards.
fact: Denticles can also be small tooth-shaped bumps on a leaf edge, an insect leg or a shell.
fact: Denticles help sharks swim fast and quietly, and stop barnacles and algae sticking to them.
fact: Engineers copy denticles, which is called biomimicry, to make swimsuits, boat hulls and hospital surfaces.
exercise: «Shark skin is covered in tiny tooth-like scales called denticles.» What is a denticle? | A deep ocean current | *A tiny tooth-like scale or bump | A large fin used for swimming | A type of seaweed
exercise: Denticles on shark skin point backwards. What do they help a shark do? | Change colour | Breathe underwater like gills | Grow a new tooth | *Swim fast and quietly
exercise: Besides shark skin, where might you find a denticle? | On a road | In a puddle | In a cloud | *On the edge of a leaf
test: Dermal denticles are found on which animal? | A lizard | A frog | A snail | *A shark
test: What do engineers copy from denticles? | Cloud shapes | The colour of seaweed | *Their shape, for swimsuits, boat hulls and hospital surfaces | The sound of waves
exam: Which word in «shark skin is covered in tiny tooth-like scales» tells you the scales are small? | skin | scales | *tiny | covered
